<title>DUBAI: Iran oil output, exports unaffected by quakes.</title>
<headline>Iran oil output, exports unaffected by quakes.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iran's oil output and export operations were unaffected by two earthquakes in northeastern Iran, Iranian and oil industry sources said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The eipcentre of the Tuesday earthquakes was outside Bojnurd near the border with Turkmenistan and Iran's Caspian coast, well away from the main oil province of Khuzestan in southwest Iran.</p>
<p>Iran produces 3.60 million barrels per day (bpd) of crude. Its exports of 2.5 million bpd making it the world's third largest exporter behind Saudi Arabia and Norway.</p>
<p>Ninety percent of its exports reach world markets through the Kharg Island offshore export terminal in the northern Gulf.</p>
</text>
